{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (actually an automated cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5260: implement `cmd/fold` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically SRD srd023-fold requirements R1.1-R1.4 (core line wrapping). This is a \"stitch\" task in generation run 44. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/fold/main.go` (the fold utility implementation) and `cmd/fold/fold_test.go` (differential tests). The implementation must match GNU `gfold` behavior byte-for-byte, verified via differential testing using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `fold` utility\n   - Differential testing: running Go binary and GNU reference binary (`gfold`) side-by-side, comparing stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` and `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for test infrastructure\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` must be called at start of main\n   - Line wrapping: splitting lines exceeding width W by inserting newlines at column boundaries\n   - Column-based width measurement (tabs expand to next 8-column tab stop) vs byte-based (-b)\n   - Default width is 80 columns\n   - `-w N` flag to set width, `-b` flag for byte mode, `-s` flag for space-break mode\n   - Task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only (core wrapping), but R1.1 references -b mode, so basic -w and -b flag parsing is needed\n   - LC_ALL=C test environment for consistent output comparison\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8 article)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines (E9 article)\n   - Write all files before building/testing (implementation strategy)\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd023-fold.yaml` (READ)\n      - Source of truth for requirements. R1.1-R1.4 define core line wrapping behavior.\n      - R1.1: Read files/stdin, wrap to W characters (columns default, bytes with -b), default 80\n      - R1.2: Lines <= max width pass through unchanged including trailing newline\n      - R1.3: Lines > max width split at exactly W columns/bytes, repeatedly applied\n      - R1.4: Final segment retains original newline if source had one; no trailing newline if source lacked one\n      - R2.1: -w N sets width (positive integer required, 0/negative = error exit 1)\n      - R2.2: Default column mode: tabs count columns to next tab stop (every 8), other control chars = 1 column\n      - R2.3: -b counts bytes, each byte = 1, disables tab-stop expansion\n      - R3.1-R3.4: -s flag breaks at last space before wrap column (fallback to hard break if no space)\n      - R4.1-R4.4: Exit codes (0 success, 1 error) and SIGPIPE handling\n      - Non-goals: no Unicode grapheme cluster width, no --help/--version beyond standard\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n      - Provides `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main()\n      ```go\n      func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n          c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n          signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n          go func() {\n              <-c\n              os.Exit(0)\n          }()\n      }\n      ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n      - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles fields\n      - RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests []DiffTest) runs each test as subtest\n      - BuildBinary referenced (from build.go, compiles cmd/ package)\n      - buildEnv sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - `cmd/fold/main.go` (TO CREATE)\n      - Main implementation of fold utility covering R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - `cmd/fold/fold_test.go` (TO CREATE)\n      - Differential tests using testutils.BuildBinary and RunDiffTests against gfold\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call was made (reading the SRD) before work was interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the full SRD to understand requirements R1.1-R1.4 and their dependencies on other requirement groups (R1.1 mentions -b flag from R2, default width of 80 from R2.1)\n   - No code has been written yet; the task is entirely pending implementation\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task specification including role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, shared_protocols, package_contracts. The task is: \"[stitch] cmd/fold: implement srd023-fold R1.1-R1.4\"\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructions to create a summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/fold/main.go` implementing srd023-fold R1.1-R1.4 (core line wrapping with -w and -b flag support, default width 80, column-based and byte-based wrapping, tab stop handling)\n   - Create `cmd/fold/fold_test.go` with differential tests against gfold reference binary\n   - Run `go build -o bin/fold ./cmd/fold/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/fold/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC2)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/fold/` to verify no issues (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd023-fold.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing the fold utility. The SRD read was the only action taken. No code has been written yet. The next step was to plan the implementation and write both `cmd/fold/main.go` and `cmd/fold/fold_test.go` before running any build/test commands.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/