{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YAeboxgddWrLcjpbDwyGe1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've gathered all the necessary information. Let me compile a comprehensive report on the patterns used in this codebase.\n\n## Key Patterns in go-unix-utils\n\n### 1. Copyright Header Format\nConsistent across all files:\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n```\n\n### 2. main.go Structure - Flag Parsing and File Processing\n\n**Entry Point Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()  // SIGPIPE handling for pipe awareness\n    os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:]))    // Exit with returned code\n}\n```\n\n**Flag Parsing Style:**\n- Manual argument parsing (no flag package) with custom `parseArgs()` function\n- Supports POSIX conventions: `-flag`, `-flagvalue`, `-flag value`, `--` separator\n- Dedicated flag parsing functions for different types:\n  - `setStyle()` for style flags (string values)\n  - `setStringOpt()` for string options\n  - `setIntOpt()` for integer options\n- Returns `(consumed int, error)` tuple - number of remaining args to skip + error\n- Single hyphen (`-`) treated as stdin, `--` marks end of flags\n- Errors formatted as `\"programname: error message\\n\"`\n\n**File Iteration Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc run(args []string) int {\n    opts, files, err := parseArgs(args)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"programname: %s\\n\", err)\n        return 1\n    }\n    if len(files) == 0 {\n        files = []string{\"-\"}  // Default to stdin\n    }\n    \n    exitCode := 0\n    for _, f := range files {\n        if err := processFile(f, opts, state, w); err != nil {\n            if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                os.Exit(0)  // Handle SIGPIPE gracefully\n            }\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"programname: %s\\n\", err)\n            exitCode = 1\n        }\n    }\n    return exitCode\n}\n```\n\n**File Processing Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc processFile(path string, opts options, state *State, w *bufio.Writer) error {\n    var r io.Reader\n    if path == \"-\" {\n        r = os.Stdin\n    } else {\n        f, err := os.Open(path)\n        if err != nil {\n            return err  // Caller wraps with program name\n        }\n        defer f.Close()\n        r = f\n    }\n    return processInput(r, opts, state, w)\n}\n```\n\n**Error Handling Pattern:**\n- Errors propagate up to `run()` function\n- `run()` handles syscall.EPIPE (pipe handling)\n- All other errors get `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"progname: %s\\n\", err)` prefix\n- Exit code 1 on error, 0 on success\n- Buffered output with explicit flush error handling\n\n### 3. Test File Structure\n\n**Test Setup Pattern:**\n```go\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n    refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gnl\")  // Reference binary lookup\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")  // Graceful skip if unavailable\n    }\n    \n    tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n        { /* test cases */ }\n    }\n    testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n**Test Case Naming:**\n- Spec-based: `\"R1.1_default_numbering\"`, `\"R2.1_body_style_a\"`\n- Descriptive of the requirement being tested\n\n**Test Organization:**\n- Separate test functions for different requirement groups (TestDiff, TestDiffR2, TestDiffFiles)\n- Fixtures created in `t.TempDir()` for file operations\n- Large file tests for SIGPIPE verification\n\n### 4. DiffTest Struct Fields\n\n```go\ntype DiffTest struct {\n    Name          string                    // Subtest name (required)\n    Args          []string                  // Command-line arguments (optional)\n    Stdin         []byte                    // Input bytes; nil=EOF, []byte{}=closed stdin\n    Env           []string                  // KEY=VALUE pairs; merged with inherited env\n    WorkDir       string                    // Working directory; defaults to t.TempDir()\n    ExitCode      int                       // Expected exit code; defaults to 0\n    Normalize     []NormalizeFunc            // Slice of normalizer functions\n    ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte         // Expected output files (relative paths)\n}\n```\n\n**Special Behaviors:**\n- `Env` nil: inherits process environment with `LC_ALL=C` override\n- `Env` non-nil: merged into inherited environment (new keys added, matching keys override)\n- `Stdin` nil vs `[]byte{}`: both produce EOF, but semantically different (nil = unopened, {} = immediately closed)\n\n### 5. Testing Utilities Functions\n\n**BuildBinary Signature:**\n```go\nfunc BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\n// Returns path to compiled binary\n// Fatal on failure\n// Uses t.TempDir() for cleanup\n// Resolves package name from directory\n```\n\n**RunDiffTests Signature:**\n```go\nfunc RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n// Runs each test as named subtest\n// Compares stdout, stderr, exit code between binaries\n// Applies normalizers before comparison\n// Uses applyNormalizers(result, normalizers) pattern\n```\n\n**Key Testing Patterns:**\n- Differential testing: Go implementation vs GNU reference binary\n- Identical inputs with comparison of outputs\n- Built-in `TimestampNormalizer` for commands with time-based output\n- `ComposeNormalizers()` for combining multiple normalizers\n- Timeout: 10 seconds default via `context.WithTimeout()`\n- Files verified via `checkExpectedFiles()` with `expectedFiles` map\n\n### 6. Options Structure Pattern\n\n```go\ntype options struct {\n    // All exported fields with defaults\n}\n\nfunc defaultOptions() options {\n    return options{\n        field1: \"defaultValue\",\n        field2: 6,\n        // ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAll configuration passed through a single `options` struct rather than globals or parameters."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dab