{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WkQeK1BugWaCNsaypuz2qX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two failures — both in the \"no trailing newline\" case. My `wrapColumnMode` is adding a trailing newline when wrapping lines that don't end with `\\n`. The issue is in how `readLine` works: when there's no newline at EOF, the line doesn't contain `\\n`, so `wrapColumnMode` should not add one. But my wrapping logic inserts `\\n` at each break point — that's correct. The problem is: the inserted `\\n` at the break becomes a trailing `\\n` when the remaining segment is written without one... wait, let me trace through.\n\nFor input `\"abcdefghij\"` with `-w 4`:\n- `readLine` returns `[]byte(\"abcdefghij\")` with no trailing newline\n- `wrapColumnMode`: line has no `\\n` at end\n- Iterates: at `i=4` (char 'e'), `col=4 > width=4`... wait, `col` would be 4 which equals width, not greater. Let me re-check.\n\nActually at `i=3`, col becomes 4 which equals width. At `i=4`, col becomes 5 > width=4. So it breaks at `i=4`. It writes `line[0:4]` = \"abcd\" then `\\n`. Then `start=4`, recalculates. At `i=8`, col becomes 5 > 4, writes `line[4:8]` = \"efgh\" then `\\n`. Then `start=8`. The remaining `line[8:]` = \"ij\" is written at the end by `w.Write(line[start:])`.\n\nThat should produce `\"abcd\\nefgh\\nij\"` with no trailing newline. But the test says it produces `\"abcd\\nefgh\\nij\\n\"`. So the issue might be in readLine adding something, or somewhere else is adding a newline.\n\nLet me check if `readLine` is the issue — when the input has no newline, `readLine` should return the bytes without `\\n`. Let me trace more carefully."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1332,"cache_read_input_tokens":35558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1332},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inferen