{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016XqRTjpABhQKYsCvZWRr3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's an extra `0a` at the end. The output is `abcd\\nefgh\\nij\\n` but should be `abcd\\nefgh\\nij`. So there's a trailing newline being added.\n\nLet me trace through the code more carefully.\n\nInput: `\"abcdefghij\"` (no trailing newline)\n\n`readLine` uses `bufio.Reader.ReadLine()`. For input without a newline, `ReadLine()` returns `(\"abcdefghij\", false, io.EOF)` — or actually, it might return the bytes on the first call with `err = nil`, and then EOF on the next call.\n\n\nI need to double-check the exact behavior of `ReadLine()` when there's no trailing newline at EOF — it should return the line content on the first call, but I'm not entirely sure how it handles the isPrefix flag and error in that case. I need to understand `bufio.ReadLine()` behavior more carefully. According to the docs, it returns the text without the line ending, and if input ends without a final newline, it still returns successfully with no error or indication—so on input like `\"abcdefghij\"`, the first call returns the entire string with `isPrefix` false and no error, then subsequent calls return EOF.\n\nThe problem with my code is that it unconditionally adds `'\\n'` whenever `ReadLine()` returns without the `isPrefix` flag, but this means I'm adding a newline to lines that originally didn't have one at EOF.\n\nSince `ReadLine()` strips the newline delimiter, I can't distinguish between a line that had a newline and one that didn't. I need to switch to `ReadBytes('\\n')` instead, which preserves the delimiter in the returned bytes and signals EOF with an error, letting me handle the two cases correctly.\n\nRewriting readLine to use ReadBytes...\n\nThis approach preserves whether each line had a trailing newline, so the first call on `\"abc\\ndef\"` returns `\"abc\\n\"` while the second returns `\"def\"` with EOF, and I can pass that information through to the wrapLine functions that need it.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":36890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":792},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dabf92a-aef3-4810-b1b9-4eb020852ade","uuid":"000dce68-e33e-454b-8ee3-b2578b6526f4"}
